  "identifier": "stardist",
  "name": "StarDist",
  "description": "Cell and nucleus instance segmentation library using star-convex polygon representations — predicts distances to object boundaries along fixed rays and refines candidates via non-maximum suppression. Supports 2D and 3D images. Widely used in computational pathology and fluorescence microscopy; natively integrated into QuPath, Fiji/ImageJ, and napari. Python package with pretrained models for H&E nuclei. Published at MICCAI 2018 (2D) and WACV 2020 (3D). Developed at MPI-CBG and EPFL. BSD-3-Clause, 1.2k stars, 272 forks, v0.9.2 (December 2025).",
  "url": "https://stardist.net/",
  "codeRepository": "https://github.com/stardist/stardist",
  "license": "BSD-3-Clause",
  "version": "0.9.2",
  "dateModified": "2025-12-15",
